# .NET Skills Routing for csharp-doctor

This workspace is wired to the `dotnet-agent-skills` marketplace (https://github.com/dotnet/skills)
via the local symlink `~/.cursor/plugins/local/dotnet-agent-skills`.

Stack snapshot (don't override without checking these):

- .NET 10 SDK (`global.json` -> `10.0.203`), `TargetFramework=net10.0`, `LangVersion=latest`
- Central Package Management enabled (`Directory.Packages.props`)
- `TreatWarningsAsErrors=true`, `Nullable=enable`, `ImplicitUsings=enable`
- Roslyn analyzers (`Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp` 4.12) in `src/CSharpDoctor.Analyzers`
- ASP.NET API in `src/CSharpDoctor.Api`
- CLI on `System.CommandLine` in `src/CSharpDoctor.Cli`
- xUnit v2 + Shouldly + NSubstitute + Testcontainers + Verify + NetArchTest

## When to reach for which skill

Always pair these with the existing `csharp-tdd-test-first.mdc` rule (tests first).

### Tests (plugin: `dotnet-test`)

| Task | Skill |
|------|-------|
| Run / filter `dotnet test`, pick VSTest vs MTP syntax | `run-tests` |
| Migrate `xunit` v2 -> `xunit.v3` (project standard) | `migrate-xunit-to-xunit-v3` |
| Move from VSTest runner to Microsoft.Testing.Platform | `migrate-vstest-to-mtp` |
| Review tests for weak / vacuous assertions | `assertion-quality` |
| Find missing coverage on changed code | `test-gap-analysis`, `coverage-analysis` |
| Smell / anti-pattern audit before merging | `test-anti-patterns`, `test-smell-detection` |
| Wrap `DateTime.UtcNow`, `File.*`, `Environment.*`, etc. for testability | `generate-testability-wrappers`, `detect-static-dependencies` |
| Categorize tests with traits / categories | `test-tagging` |

### Build & packages (plugins: `dotnet-msbuild`, `dotnet-nuget`)

| Task | Skill |
|------|-------|
| Read a `.binlog` and explain a failure | `dotnet-msbuild/binlog-failure-analysis` |
| Slow build investigation | `dotnet-msbuild/build-perf-diagnostics`, `eval-performance`, `incremental-build`, `build-parallelism` |
| Audit / refactor `Directory.Build.props` | `dotnet-msbuild/directory-build-organization`, `property-patterns`, `item-management`, `msbuild-antipatterns` |
| Custom MSBuild targets / extension points (this repo ships a Roslyn analyzer + Sarif) | `target-authoring`, `extension-points`, `including-generated-files` |
| Drift / version conflicts across CPM | `dotnet-nuget/convert-to-cpm` (also re-aligns versions when already on CPM) |

### Analyzer / Roslyn / general C# (plugin: `dotnet`)

| Task | Skill |
|------|-------|
| Throwaway `.cs` repro or quick API probe (don't add to solution) | `csharp-scripts` |
| P/Invoke / native interop questions | `dotnet-pinvoke` |
| Publishing the analyzer / CLI to NuGet via Trusted Publishing | `nuget-trusted-publishing` |

### ASP.NET API (plugin: `dotnet-aspnet`)

Use for changes inside `src/CSharpDoctor.Api`:

- `dotnet-webapi` for endpoint shape / minimal API patterns
- `minimal-api-file-upload` for inspection upload endpoints
- `configuring-opentelemetry-dotnet` if/when telemetry is added

### Diagnostics / perf (plugin: `dotnet-diag`)

Analyzer perf and CLI perf belong here:

- `analyzing-dotnet-performance`, `microbenchmarking`, `dotnet-trace-collect`, `dump-collect`

### Upgrades (plugin: `dotnet-upgrade`)

- Already on .NET 10 -> use `migrate-dotnet10-to-dotnet11` only when explicitly bumping
- `migrate-nullable-references` if a project ever flips `Nullable` off->on
- `dotnet-aot-compat` before publishing the CLI as Native AOT

### Skills NOT relevant here (do not load)

`dotnet-blazor`, `dotnet-maui`, `dotnet-ai`, `dotnet-data`, `dotnet-template-engine` (unless we
start shipping `dotnet new` templates), `dotnet-experimental`.

## Notes & gotchas

- The `dotnet` plugin bundles an LSP config (`lsp.json`) launching `roslyn-language-server` via
  `dotnet dnx`. If you already have the C# Dev Kit / OmniSharp wired in Cursor, only enable one
  to avoid duplicate diagnostics.
- The marketplace is a **symlink** -- run `cd ~/.cursor/plugins/sources/dotnet-skills && git pull`
  to refresh; no need to re-link.
- After installing/uninstalling plugins, run `Developer: Reload Window` in Cursor.
